From 845d19b5e76c7ad777da87d71531e2082f81c26a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nex <63727521+LuCiLuna@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:19:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 150/167] HACK: soc: qcom: handle the OnePlus 9 in the bring-up splash
 path

op9-splash-autorefresh() returns early unless the machine is a 9 Pro, which
also skips disabling the Gunyah watchdog. On the OnePlus 9 that watchdog
resets the phone about ten seconds after handoff, so the gate has to accept
oneplus,lemonade as well. The DSI INTF addresses it writes are SoC-level.
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/op9-splash-autorefresh.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/op9-splash-autorefresh.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/op9-splash-autorefresh.c
index c5582dda5..8c2ff9019 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/op9-splash-autorefresh.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/op9-splash-autorefresh.c
@@ -58,7 +58,8 @@ static int __init op9_splash_autorefresh(void)
 {
 	int i;
 
-	if (!of_machine_is_compatible("oneplus,lemonadep"))
+	if (!of_machine_is_compatible("oneplus,lemonadep") &&
+	    !of_machine_is_compatible("oneplus,lemonade"))
 		return 0;
 
 	/*
